== 3.7 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Variation that shows a continuous range of values, such as height, is called],
  [adaptation],
  [mutation],
  [discontinuous variation],
  [continuous variation]
)

#mcq(2, [Which of the following shows discontinuous variation?],
  [Blood group],
  [Leaf length],
  [Body mass],
  [Height]
)

#mcq(3, [Continuous variation is controlled mainly by],
  [a single gene],
  [many genes acting together],
  [the environment only],
  [mutations in one gene]
)

#mcq(4, [The main source of new alleles in a population is],
  [meiosis],
  [crossing over],
  [fertilisation],
  [mutation]
)

#mcq(5, [A change in the base sequence of DNA is called a],
  [mutation],
  [replication],
  [transcription],
  [translation]
)

#mcq(6, [A mutation that changes a single base in a gene is a],
  [genomic mutation],
  [chromosome mutation],
  [frameshift mutation],
  [gene mutation]
)

#mcq(7, [Down syndrome is caused by],
  [a gene mutation],
  [an extra chromosome 21],
  [a missing sex chromosome],
  [crossing over]
)

#mcq(8, [Sickle-cell anaemia results from],
  [a chromosome deletion],
  [a single base substitution in the haemoglobin gene],
  [crossing over],
  [an extra chromosome]
)

#mcq(9, [Which of these is a chromosome mutation?],
  [Sickle-cell anaemia],
  [Albinism],
  [Down syndrome caused by translocation],
  [Colour blindness]
)

#mcq(10, [A mutation that has no effect on the phenotype is described as],
  [lethal],
  [neutral],
  [harmful],
  [beneficial]
)

#mcq(11, [Most mutations are harmful because],
  [they disturb a protein that was working well],
  [they are always dominant],
  [they occur only in gametes],
  [they always delete a chromosome]
)

#mcq(12, [A mutation in a body cell is not passed to offspring because],
  [it is always recessive],
  [body cells do not divide],
  [it is not in the gametes],
  [it is corrected at once]
)

#mcq(13, [An example of a mutation that is useful to humans is],
  [a human with sickle-cell anaemia],
  [a mouse without fur],
  [a plant variety that resists a disease],
  [albinism in a mammal]
)

#mcq(14, [Sickle-cell heterozygotes survive malaria better than homozygotes. This is an example of],
  [heterozygote advantage],
  [sex linkage],
  [neutral mutation],
  [complete dominance]
)

#mcq(15, [The sickle-cell allele is common in West Africa because],
  [it causes no harm],
  [it is on the X chromosome],
  [it is dominant],
  [it protects heterozygotes against malaria]
)

#mcq(16, [A feature that helps an organism survive in its habitat is an],
  [mutation],
  [variation],
  [adaptation],
  [acclimatisation]
)

#mcq(17, [A cactus is adapted to a dry habitat by],
  [broad thin leaves],
  [rapid transpiration],
  [leaves reduced to spines and a thick water-storing stem],
  [shallow roots only]
)

#mcq(18, [Which of these is a behavioural adaptation?],
  [Long roots],
  [Thick fur],
  [Waxy leaf cuticle],
  [Migration of birds]
)

#mcq(19, [Which of these is a physiological adaptation?],
  [Sharp claws],
  [Hibernation body-temperature drop],
  [Camouflage colour],
  [Long legs]
)

#mcq(20, [The changes a plant makes during its own life in response to its habitat are],
  [mutations],
  [acclimatisation],
  [variations],
  [adaptations]
)

#mcq(21, [Organisms with favourable variations are more likely to survive and reproduce. This is],
  [speciation],
  [natural selection],
  [artificial selection],
  [mutation]
)

#mcq(22, [Selection by humans of the plants and animals they find useful is],
  [artificial selection],
  [natural selection],
  [speciation],
  [adaptation]
)

#mcq(23, [Which statement about variation is correct?],
  [All variation is inherited],
  [Variation occurs only in plants],
  [Some variation is caused by the environment],
  [Variation is always harmful]
)

#mcq(24, [Identical twins differ slightly because of],
  [different chromosomes],
  [different genes],
  [different sexes],
  [environmental effects]
)

#mcq(25, [A mutation that changes one base and alters all the following codons is a],
  [silent mutation],
  [frameshift mutation],
  [point mutation],
  [chromosome mutation]
)

#mcq(26, [The agent that increases the rate of mutation is called a],
  [mutagen],
  [gene],
  [catalyst],
  [vector]
)

#mcq(27, [Which does *not* cause mutation?],
  [Some chemicals in tobacco smoke],
  [X-rays],
  [Ultraviolet radiation],
  [Crossing over]
)

#mcq(28, [Variation within a species is important because it],
  [reduces the gene pool],
  [prevents reproduction],
  [gives natural selection something to act on],
  [makes the species uniform]
)

#mcq(29, [A population in which every individual is genetically identical is at risk because],
  [it grows too slowly],
  [it has too many alleles],
  [it cannot reproduce],
  [a single disease may wipe it out]
)

#mcq(30, [An adaptation to living in water is],
  [a waxy cuticle],
  [thick fur],
  [spines instead of leaves],
  [a streamlined body and gills]
)

