  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Continuous variation is measured, not counted, and is controlled by many genes.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Blood group falls into a few distinct classes with nothing in between.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Polygenes each add a small effect, and the environment smooths the result into a range.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Mutation is the only process that creates a genuinely new allele.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Mutations change the code itself, and may or may not change the protein.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A point (gene) mutation alters one base or a few bases within a gene.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Nondisjunction in meiosis gives three copies of chromosome 21 — a trisomy.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    One base change substitutes valine for glutamic acid, and the haemoglobin molecules stick together.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A translocation moves a piece of one chromosome to another — a change in chromosome structure.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Neutral mutations occur in non-coding DNA or do not change the amino acid sequence.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A random change to a working code usually damages the product rather than improving it.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Only mutations in the germ line are inherited.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Breeders and farmers use useful mutations, and mutation breeding creates them deliberately.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Carrying one sickle allele gives some protection against malaria, so the allele persists in the population.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Natural selection keeps the allele where malaria is common, because carriers survive better.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    An adaptation is an inherited feature produced by natural selection.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Spines reduce water loss and also protect the stem; the stem stores water and photosynthesises.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Behaviour is what the organism does, not what it is built of.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Physiological adaptations are internal processes such as a lowered metabolic rate.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Acclimatisation is temporary and is not inherited.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Natural selection is the differential survival of naturally occurring variants.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Farmers and breeders choose the parents, so the change is directed by human need.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Body mass, leaf size and skin colour are all affected by the environment as well as by genes.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The genotype is the same, so the differences are environmental.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Inserting or deleting a base shifts the reading frame, so every codon after it changes.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Radiation, some chemicals and some viruses are mutagens.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Crossing over reshuffles existing alleles; it does not create new ones.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Without variation there is no differential survival, so evolution cannot happen.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Genetic uniformity means no individual has a variant that could resist a new disease.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Streamlining reduces drag and gills extract dissolved oxygen.
  ]

]

